new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4699fd6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/asar_repro/docs/stdc_window_improvement.md
@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+# Fixed-time window improvement for STDC (research, 2026-11-23)
+
+This experiment addresses complete-route quality under a finite computation
+budget. It adds independent modules; the frozen scorer, motion input, planning
+objective, legacy A^SAR, baseline branch and earlier reports are unchanged.
+Results belong to a new protocol, not an amendment of B7 or old STDC runs.
+
+## Objective and exact suffix
+
+The original objective remains `J = sum(M[t], t=1..T)` and final detection is
+`Pd = 1-M[T]`. Frame zero is not observed. Minimizing J does not mathematically
+imply maximizing final Pd; the two are measured separately. Acceptance requires
+full-path J improvement greater than 1e-10, without adding a Pd constraint.
+
+For a window [a,b], the prefix through a, the vertex at b, the absolute clock,
+and the suffix after b remain fixed. Every candidate retains its entire belief
+vector; equal (depth, vertex) or equal total mass do not identify a state.
+
+Let D_t attenuate the searched cell/particle IDs at absolute frame t. Matrix
+motion uses source-row stochastic P_t and b_t = D_t P_t^T b_(t-1). Define
+nonnegative fixed-suffix vectors c_T=0, s_T=1 and work backwards:
+
+    c_(t-1) = P_t D_t (1 + c_t)
+    s_(t-1) = P_t D_t s_t
+
+For particles the position sequence is already fixed, so P is replaced by the
+identity on ID-indexed weights and D_t uses cell_ids[t]. Special bins retain
+their mass and have attenuation factor 1. Then for every rewritten window:
+
+    J_full = g_a + J_window + c_b^T b'_b
+    Pd_full = 1 - s_b^T b'_b
+
+Every accepted route and every returned incumbent is independently replayed by
+the unchanged full-path scorer. Coefficient/replay disagreement above 1e-10 is
+an assertion failure, never silently corrected.
+
+## Bounds and their limited scope
+
+Four local controls use the same feasible paths and schedule: zero, mass_lb,
+stdc_lb, stdc_endpoint_lb. Terminal bounds include the exact fixed-suffix cost.
+All modes exclude prefixes unable to reach the endpoint in exactly R steps.
+
+At relative step k, ordinary STDC relaxes to all vertices exactly k moves away.
+Endpoint STDC intersects that set with vertices exactly R-k moves from the
+endpoint. The zero-step set contains only its source; no wait action is added.
+Every legal completion is included in these sets. Simultaneously observing
+each set yields a componentwise lower undetected belief. The original STDC
+per-step mass recurrence lower-bounds window cost. Adding c_b dotted with the
+final relaxed belief lower-bounds the fixed suffix because c_b is nonnegative.
+These arguments require fixed nonnegative mass-preserving motion, fixed
+nonnegative detection probabilities in [0,1], and the supplied discrete grid.
+Random Oracle checks are finite numerical evidence, not a general proof.
+
+Local search is unweighted best-first and uses a conservative numerical bound
+guard at incumbent J + 1e-10. A completed window exhausts its endpoint-constrained
+neighborhood up to the acceptance tolerance. Neither that completion nor an
+unchanged whole sweep certifies a global optimum or global epsilon bound.
+`theory_certified` is always false for this composite method. Original dynamic
+paper_greedy remains uncertified, including when its search completes.
+
+## Predeclared experimental allocation
+
+All real methods receive the same frozen PT route as a supplied common input.
+Its historical construction is not re-run or timed. Baseline paper_greedy gets
+the total 5000 expansion / 20000 physical OPEN / 30 second search budget.
+Each window method spends at most 1500 of those expansions on its own paper
+seed, then uses the remaining shared budget for windows. Seed computation,
+coefficient construction, local search, accepted-route replay and final replay
+are all timed. An expansion subquota stop can continue locally; a global time
+or OPEN stop cannot. This allocation is part of the proposed method, so the
+baseline comparison includes an allocation difference. The four window
+controls isolate the contribution of the local STDC bounds more directly.
+
+The seed uses epsilon in {1.1,1.04,1.0}; local windows have no epsilon inflation.
+Scan lengths 4 then 6, starts in increasing order; after each accepted rewrite,
+subsequent windows rebuild beliefs and suffix coefficients from the new route.
+Repeat sweeps until an entire sweep has no accepted improvement or a global
+budget stops the process. There is no undisclosed iteration cap. Full routes
+found just before a cooperative stop are retained. Overshoot is recorded.
+
+Expanded counts sum across phases. Generated counts exclude roots and count
+materialized child states; infeasible endpoints can be rejected geometrically
+before materialization. Pruned counts include such geometry rejections. OPEN
+is the maximum physical heap size across sequential phases, not their sum.
+Window heuristic/candidate/replay counters describe only the local phase; seed
+legacy counters are reported separately. Process peak memory includes input
+verification and final external replay in an isolated worker.
+
+## Sequential gates and interpretation
+
+1. New hand-calculated, indexing, suffix, budget and Oracle unit tests.
+2. Full existing regression suite, with no skips or xfails introduced.
+3. 160 random matrix/particle toy cases, every legal window prefix vs independent DFS.
+4. 35 unchanged historical small cases plus 5 stationary and 5 particle
+   derivatives, two windows and four modes (360 searches).
+5. Frozen real archive/forcing/scorer SHA verification and six smoke runs.
+6. 45 paired real runs: five methods, three epsilons, three repetitions.
+
+Any historical test, admissibility or replay failure blocks later stages.
+Every stage retains command, seed, stderr, JSON, source fingerprints and diff.
+Real data never use synthetic replacement. Earlier baseline and result files
+are checked byte-for-byte before and after the run. Conclusions distinguish
+route improvement, bound-specific improvement, budget effects and unverified
+generalization beyond the single frozen scenario. Global anytime/MHA changes,
+new forcing, a changed objective and a second innovation are out of scope.

diff --git a/asar_repro/scripts/audit_window_bounds.py b/asar_repro/scripts/audit_window_bounds.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9208752
--- /dev/null
+++ b/asar_repro/scripts/audit_window_bounds.py
@@ -0,0 +1,393 @@
+"""Independent exhaustive fixed-window audit on reproducible synthetic toys.
+
+The Oracle enumerates complete legal paths with the original prefix, endpoint,
+absolute window times, and suffix. Every candidate is replayed by the frozen
+``score_path`` evaluator. Neither bounds, suffix coefficients, nor reachability
+helpers determine the Oracle's routes or costs.
+
+This is a finite numerical audit of a fixed-window problem. It is not a proof
+of a global epsilon guarantee or an evaluation on real forcing/particles.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+from dataclasses import dataclass
+import hashlib
+import json
+import math
+from pathlib import Path
+import sys
+import traceback
+
+import numpy as np
+
+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
+sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / "src"))
+
+from asar_repro.grid import GridGraph
+from asar_repro.motion import MatrixMotion, ParticleMotion
+from asar_repro.objective import PathScore, score_path
+from asar_repro.window_bounds import WindowHeuristic, suffix_coefficients
+
+
+MODES = ("zero", "mass_lb", "stdc_lb", "stdc_endpoint_lb")
+TOLERANCE = 1e-10
+SEEDS = tuple(range(100, 180))
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class ToyCase:
+    kind: str
+    seed: int
+    grid: GridGraph
+    reference_path: tuple[int, ...]
+    window_start: int
+    window_end: int
+    p: np.ndarray
+    q: float | np.ndarray
+    motion: MatrixMotion | ParticleMotion
+    motion_label: str
+
+    @property
+    def horizon(self):
+        return len(self.reference_path) - 1
+
+
+@dataclass
+class WindowOracle:
+    candidates: dict[tuple[int, ...], PathScore]
+    best_full_J_by_prefix: dict[tuple[int, ...], float]
+    best_full_path_by_prefix: dict[tuple[int, ...], tuple[int, ...]]
+
+
+def _validate_case(case):
+    case.grid.validate_path(case.reference_path, start=case.reference_path[0],
+                            budget=case.horizon)
+    if not 0 <= case.window_start <= case.window_end <= case.horizon:
+        raise ValueError("window must satisfy 0 <= a <= b <= T")
+
+
+def replay(case, path, *, record_beliefs=True):
+    """Use the original initial state and absolute times for every replay."""
+    return score_path(case.grid, path, start=case.reference_path[0],
+                      budget=len(path) - 1, p=case.p, q=case.q,
+                      motion=case.motion, record_beliefs=record_beliefs)
+
+
+def legal_window_prefixes(case):
+    """All legal prefixes, including ones unable to reach the fixed endpoint."""
+    _validate_case(case)
+    route = list(case.reference_path[:case.window_start + 1])
+
+    def visit():
+        yield tuple(route)
+        if len(route) - 1 == case.window_end:
+            return
+        for vertex in case.grid.neighbors(route[-1]):
+            route.append(vertex)
+            yield from visit()
+            route.pop()
+
+    yield from visit()
+
+
+def enumerate_window_oracle(case):
+    """Independent DFS of every same-time, same-endpoint replacement.
+
+    No state merging occurs: different route histories remain different keys,
+    even when their (depth, vertex), total mass, or cost happen to coincide.
+    No bound, backward coefficient, or production reachability helper is used.
+    """
+    _validate_case(case)
+    candidates = {}
+    best_costs = {}
+    best_paths = {}
+    route = list(case.reference_path[:case.window_start + 1])
+    endpoint = case.reference_path[case.window_end]
+
+    def visit():
+        if len(route) - 1 == case.window_end:
+            if route[-1] != endpoint:
+                return
+            full_path = tuple(route) + case.reference_path[case.window_end + 1:]
+            score = replay(case, full_path)
+            candidates[full_path] = score
+            for depth in range(case.window_start, case.window_end + 1):
+                prefix = full_path[:depth + 1]
+                if score.J < best_costs.get(prefix, math.inf):
+                    best_costs[prefix] = score.J
+                    best_paths[prefix] = full_path
+            return
+        for vertex in case.grid.neighbors(route[-1]):
+            route.append(vertex)
+            visit()
+            route.pop()
+
+    visit()
+    return WindowOracle(candidates, best_costs, best_paths)
+
+
+def make_random_case(kind, seed):
+    """Seed is sufficient to rebuild every input; no external data are used."""
+    if kind not in ("matrix", "particle"):
+        raise ValueError("kind must be matrix or particle")
+    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)
+    rows, cols = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 3))[seed % 3]
+    grid = GridGraph(rows, cols)
+    horizon = 4 + seed % 2
+    route = [int(rng.integers(grid.size))]
+    for _ in range(horizon):
+        route.append(int(rng.choice(grid.neighbors(route[-1]))))
+    a = seed % 2
+    b = horizon - int(seed % 4 < 2)
+    sensor_kind = seed % 4
+    if sensor_kind == 0:
+        q = 0.0
+    elif sensor_kind == 1:
+        q = 1.0
+    elif sensor_kind == 2:
+        q = rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95, grid.size)
+        q[0], q[-1] = 0.0, 1.0
+    else:
+        q = 0.78
+    if kind == "matrix":
+        if seed % 4 == 0:
+            motion = MatrixMotion.identity(grid.size)
+            label = "static_identity"
+        elif seed % 4 == 1:
+            matrix = rng.dirichlet(np.ones(grid.size), grid.size)
+            motion = MatrixMotion.stationary(matrix)
+            label = "stationary_asymmetric"
+        else:
+            matrices = [rng.dirichlet(np.ones(grid.size), grid.size)
+                        for _ in range(horizon)]
+            motion = MatrixMotion.time_varying(matrices)
+            label = "time_varying_asymmetric"
+        p = rng.dirichlet(np.ones(grid.size))
+    else:
+        count = grid.size + 6
+        cells = rng.integers(0, grid.size + 4, size=(horizon + 1, count))
+        # Four persistent special-bin trajectories cannot be sensed by a route.
+        cells[:, -4:] = grid.size + np.arange(4)
+        ids = rng.permutation(count) * 17 + seed * 1000
+        motion = ParticleMotion(cells, grid.size, ids)
+        label = "synthetic_id_preserving_with_four_special_bins"
+        p = rng.dirichlet(np.ones(count))
+    return ToyCase(kind, seed, grid, tuple(route), a, b, p, q, motion, label)
+
+
+def case_payload(case):
+    payload = {
+        "kind": case.kind, "seed": case.seed, "data_type": "synthetic_toy",
+        "motion_label": case.motion_label,
+        "grid": {"rows": case.grid.rows, "cols": case.grid.cols},
+        "reference_path": list(case.reference_path),
+        "window": [case.window_start, case.window_end],
+        "p": case.p.tolist(), "q": np.asarray(case.q).tolist(),
+        "t0_convention": "frame zero has no observation; first motion/sense is t=1",
+    }
+    if isinstance(case.motion, MatrixMotion):
+        payload["motion"] = {
+            "repeat": case.motion._repeat,
+            "matrices": [matrix.toarray().tolist() for matrix in case.motion._matrices],
+        }
+    else:
+        payload["motion"] = {
+            "cell_ids": case.motion.cell_ids.tolist(),
+            "trajectory_ids": case.motion.trajectory_ids.tolist(),
+            "special_bins": case.motion.bin_count - case.motion.size,
+        }
+    return payload
+
+
+def audit_case(case, *, record=None):
+    """Check every legal internal prefix against the complete replay Oracle.
+
+    ``record`` receives the numerical evidence before any assertions, so the
+    last-check file identifies the failing prefix if a gate fails.
+    """
+    oracle = enumerate_window_oracle(case)
+    if not oracle.candidates:
+        raise AssertionError("valid reference path must provide a window completion")
+    coefficients = suffix_coefficients(case.grid, case.reference_path,
+                                       q=case.q, motion=case.motion)
+    tail = coefficients.cost[case.window_end]
+    heuristics = {
+        mode: WindowHeuristic(case.grid,
+                              end_vertex=case.reference_path[case.window_end],
+                              end_depth=case.window_end, q=case.q,
+                              motion=case.motion, tail_cost=tail, mode=mode)
+        for mode in MODES
+    }
+    max_cost_error = 0.0
+    max_survival_error = 0.0
+    # Only the fixed suffix (d >= b) is common to different window candidates.
+    # For the reference, every depth can additionally be checked.
+    suffix_checks = 0
+    for path, score in oracle.candidates.items():
+        depths = (range(case.horizon + 1) if path == case.reference_path
+                  else range(case.window_end, case.horizon + 1))
+        for depth in depths:
+            J_from_suffix = float(score.g[depth] + coefficients.cost[depth] @ score.beliefs[depth])
+            mass_from_suffix = float(coefficients.survival[depth] @ score.beliefs[depth])
+            cost_error = abs(J_from_suffix - score.J)
+            survival_error = abs(mass_from_suffix - score.survival[-1])
+            evidence = {
+                "check": "suffix_linearity", "kind": case.kind, "seed": case.seed,
+                "path": list(path), "depth": depth,
+                "J_replay": score.J, "J_from_suffix": J_from_suffix,
+                "final_mass_replay": float(score.survival[-1]),
+                "final_mass_from_suffix": mass_from_suffix,
+                "cost_error": cost_error, "survival_error": survival_error,
+            }
+            if record:
+                record(evidence)
+            assert cost_error <= TOLERANCE, evidence
+            assert survival_error <= TOLERANCE, evidence
+            max_cost_error = max(max_cost_error, cost_error)
+            max_survival_error = max(max_survival_error, survival_error)
+            suffix_checks += 1
+
+    feasible = 0
+    infeasible = 0
+    max_overestimate = {mode: 0.0 for mode in MODES}
+    minimum_endpoint_margin = math.inf
+    for prefix in legal_window_prefixes(case):
+        depth = len(prefix) - 1
+        prefix_score = replay(case, prefix)
+        best_full_J = oracle.best_full_J_by_prefix.get(prefix, math.inf)
+        remaining = best_full_J - prefix_score.J
+        values = {mode: float(heuristic(prefix[-1], depth, prefix_score.final_belief))
+                  for mode, heuristic in heuristics.items()}
+        possible = math.isfinite(remaining)
+        evidence = {
+            "check": "prefix_admissibility", "kind": case.kind, "seed": case.seed,
+            "window": [case.window_start, case.window_end],
+            "prefix": list(prefix), "depth": depth, "feasible": possible,
+            "prefix_J": prefix_score.J,
+            "oracle_remaining": remaining if possible else None,
+            "oracle_best_full_path": list(oracle.best_full_path_by_prefix[prefix]) if possible else None,
+            "h": {mode: value if math.isfinite(value) else None
+                  for mode, value in values.items()},
+            "h_is_positive_infinity": {mode: value == math.inf for mode, value in values.items()},
+        }
+        if record:
+            record(evidence)
+        if not possible:
+            assert all(value == math.inf for value in values.values()), evidence
+            infeasible += 1
+            continue
+        feasible += 1
+        for mode, value in values.items():
+            assert math.isfinite(value), evidence
+            assert value >= -TOLERANCE, evidence
+            assert value <= remaining + TOLERANCE, evidence
+            if depth == case.window_end:
+                assert abs(value - remaining) <= TOLERANCE, evidence
+            max_overestimate[mode] = max(max_overestimate[mode], value - remaining)
+        margin = values["stdc_endpoint_lb"] - values["stdc_lb"]
+        assert margin >= -TOLERANCE, evidence
+        minimum_endpoint_margin = min(minimum_endpoint_margin, margin)
+
+    return {
+        "kind": case.kind, "seed": case.seed, "motion_label": case.motion_label,
+        "candidate_paths": len(oracle.candidates), "feasible_prefixes": feasible,
+        "infeasible_prefixes": infeasible, "suffix_linearity_checks": suffix_checks,
+        "max_admissibility_overestimate": max_overestimate,
+        "minimum_endpoint_minus_plain": minimum_endpoint_margin,
+        "max_suffix_cost_error": max_cost_error,
+        "max_suffix_survival_error": max_survival_error,
+        "status": "passed",
+    }
+
+
+def _save(path, value):
+    path.write_text(json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2, allow_nan=False) + "\n",
+                    encoding="utf-8")
+
+
+def _fingerprint(path):
+    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
+
+
+def main(argv=None):
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
+    parser.add_argument("--output-dir", type=Path, required=True,
+                        help="new directory, or an existing empty directory")
+    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
+    output = args.output_dir.resolve()
+    if output.exists() and (not output.is_dir() or any(output.iterdir())):
+        raise FileExistsError(f"refusing to overwrite nonempty audit output: {output}")
+    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    inputs = output / "inputs"
+    inputs.mkdir()
+    _save(output / "protocol.json", {
+        "command": [sys.executable, str(Path(__file__).resolve()), *sys.argv[1:]],
+        "seeds_per_kind": list(SEEDS), "kinds": ["matrix", "particle"],
+        "expected_cases": 160, "tolerance": TOLERANCE,
+        "data_type": "synthetic_toy", "oracle": "independent DFS plus full frozen score_path replay",
+        "scope": "fixed absolute-time window, endpoint, prefix and suffix",
+        "global_epsilon_certified": False,
+        "source_sha256": {str(path.relative_to(ROOT)): _fingerprint(path) for path in (
+            Path(__file__).resolve(), ROOT / "src/asar_repro/window_bounds.py",
+            ROOT / "src/asar_repro/objective.py", ROOT / "src/asar_repro/motion.py",
+        )},
+    })
+    results = []
+    current = None
+    record_count = 0
+    try:
+        with (output / "checks.jsonl").open("w", encoding="utf-8") as stream:
+            def record(evidence):
+                nonlocal record_count
+                record_count += 1
+                evidence = {"record_index": record_count, **evidence}
+                stream.write(json.dumps(evidence, ensure_ascii=False, allow_nan=False) + "\n")
+                stream.flush()
+                _save(output / "last_checked.json", evidence)
+
+            for kind in ("matrix", "particle"):
+                for seed in SEEDS:
+                    current = {"kind": kind, "seed": seed}
+                    case = make_random_case(kind, seed)
+                    _save(inputs / f"{kind}_{seed}.json", case_payload(case))
+                    _save(output / "last_checked.json", {"check": "case_start", **current})
+                    results.append(audit_case(case, record=record))
+                    if len(results) % 20 == 0:
+                        print(f"validated {len(results)}/160 synthetic window cases", flush=True)
+        summary = {
+            "status": "passed", "case_count": len(results), "expected_cases": 160,
+            "seeds_per_kind": list(SEEDS), "tolerance": TOLERANCE,
+            "data_type": "synthetic_toy", "global_epsilon_certified": False,
+            "scope": "numerical admissibility and suffix replay for the fixed-window model only",
+            "check_records": record_count,
+            "candidate_paths": sum(row["candidate_paths"] for row in results),
+            "feasible_prefixes": sum(row["feasible_prefixes"] for row in results),
+            "infeasible_prefixes": sum(row["infeasible_prefixes"] for row in results),
+            "max_admissibility_overestimate": {
+                mode: max(row["max_admissibility_overestimate"][mode] for row in results)
+                for mode in MODES},
+            "max_suffix_cost_error": max(row["max_suffix_cost_error"] for row in results),
+            "max_suffix_survival_error": max(row["max_suffix_survival_error"] for row in results),
+            "minimum_endpoint_minus_plain": min(row["minimum_endpoint_minus_plain"] for row in results),
+            "cases": results,
+        }
+        assert len(results) == 160, "incomplete audit"
+        _save(output / "summary.json", summary)
+        print(json.dumps({key: summary[key] for key in ("status", "case_count", "feasible_prefixes",
+                                                       "infeasible_prefixes", "max_suffix_cost_error")},
+                         ensure_ascii=False, allow_nan=False), flush=True)
+    except Exception as exc:
+        _save(output / "summary.json", {
+            "status": "blocked", "completed_cases": len(results), "current_case": current,
+            "error_type": type(exc).__name__, "error": str(exc),
+            "global_epsilon_certified": False, "cases": results,
+        })
+        (output / "failure_traceback.txt").write_text(traceback.format_exc(), encoding="utf-8")
+        print(f"blocked: {type(exc).__name__}: {exc}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
+        raise
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()

diff --git a/asar_repro/scripts/audit_window_search.py b/asar_repro/scripts/audit_window_search.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f98cee8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/asar_repro/scripts/audit_window_search.py
@@ -0,0 +1,271 @@
+"""Fail-fast fixed-window search audit against independent full-path DFS.
+
+The 35 historical small_case inputs (seeds 15000..15034) are unchanged.
+Five stationary-matrix and five synthetic-particle derivatives are explicitly
+additional cases. No real archive or forcing is substituted by these toys.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+from dataclasses import asdict, is_dataclass
+import hashlib
+import json
+import math
+from pathlib import Path
+import sys
+from time import perf_counter
+import traceback
+
+import numpy as np
+
+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
+sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / "src"))
+
+from asar_repro.motion import MatrixMotion, ParticleMotion
+from asar_repro.objective import score_path
+from asar_repro.window_search import solve_window
+from stdc_validation_guards import freeze_case, small_case
+
+
+MODES = ("zero", "mass_lb", "stdc_lb", "stdc_endpoint_lb")
+ATOL = 1e-10
+HISTORICAL_SEEDS = tuple(range(15000, 15035))
+DERIVED_SEEDS = tuple(range(15000, 15005))
+
+
+def _require(condition, message):
+    if not condition:
+        raise AssertionError(message)
+
+
+def _native(value):
+    if isinstance(value, np.ndarray):
+        return value.tolist()
+    if isinstance(value, np.generic):
+        return value.item()
+    if isinstance(value, dict):
+        return {str(key): _native(item) for key, item in value.items()}
+    if isinstance(value, (tuple, list)):
+        return [_native(item) for item in value]
+    return value
+
+
+def _save(path, value):
+    path.write_text(json.dumps(_native(value), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2,
+                               allow_nan=False) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
+
+
+def _sha(path):
+    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
+
+
+def cases():
+    """Retain all 35 original inputs, then add labelled motion derivatives."""
+    for seed in HISTORICAL_SEEDS:
+        grid, cfg = small_case(seed)
+        yield "historical_dynamic_matrix", seed, grid, cfg, "unchanged small_case(seed)"
+    for seed in DERIVED_SEEDS:
+        grid, cfg = small_case(seed)
+        derived = {**cfg, "motion": MatrixMotion.stationary(cfg["motion"]._matrices[0])}
+        yield ("derived_stationary_matrix", seed, grid, derived,
+               "repeat the historical first transition kernel; retain grid, p, q, start and T")
+    for seed in DERIVED_SEEDS:
+        grid, cfg = small_case(seed)
+        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed + 2_000_000)
+        count = 8
+        cells = rng.integers(0, grid.size, size=(cfg["budget"] + 1, count))
+        cells[:, -4:] = grid.size + np.arange(4)
+        ids = seed * 100 + np.array([31, 4, 77, 2, 91, 8, 65, 19])
+        derived = {**cfg, "p": rng.dirichlet(np.ones(count)),
+                   "motion": ParticleMotion(cells, grid.size, ids)}
+        yield ("derived_synthetic_particle", seed, grid, derived,
+               "eight synthetic ID trajectories with four persistent special bins; retain grid, q, start and T")
+
+
+def reference_path(grid, cfg, seed):
+    """An unoptimized deterministic route; no objective-dependent selection."""
+    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed + 1_000_000)
+    route = [cfg["start"]]
+    for _ in range(cfg["budget"]):
+        route.append(int(rng.choice(grid.neighbors(route[-1]))))
+    return tuple(route)
+
+
+def independent_window_oracle(grid, cfg, path, a, b):
+    """Exhaust all legal same-endpoint routes, replaying each full candidate.
+
+    The enumerator never calls production reachability, bounds, coefficients,
+    window search, or search-state merging. It preserves original absolute
+    times by splicing each candidate into the full original path.
+    """
+    grid.validate_path(path, start=cfg["start"], budget=cfg["budget"])
+    _require(0 <= a <= b <= cfg["budget"], "invalid Oracle window")
+    route = list(path[:a + 1])
+    best_J = math.inf
+    best_path = None
+    candidates = 0
+
+    def visit():
+        nonlocal best_J, best_path, candidates
+        if len(route) - 1 == b:
+            if route[-1] != path[b]:
+                return
+            candidate = tuple(route) + path[b + 1:]
+            score = score_path(grid, candidate, **cfg)
+            candidates += 1
+            if score.J < best_J:
+                best_J, best_path = score.J, candidate
+            return
+        for vertex in grid.neighbors(route[-1]):
+            route.append(vertex)
+            visit()
+            route.pop()
+
+    visit()
+    _require(candidates > 0 and best_path is not None,
+             "the valid reference must be a feasible Oracle candidate")
+    return {"J": best_J, "path": best_path, "candidate_count": candidates}
+
+
+def main(argv=None):
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
+    parser.add_argument("--output-dir", type=Path, required=True,
+                        help="a new directory or an existing empty directory")
+    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
+    output = args.output_dir.resolve()
+    if output.exists() and (not output.is_dir() or any(output.iterdir())):
+        raise FileExistsError(f"refusing to overwrite nonempty output: {output}")
+    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    inputs = output / "inputs"
+    inputs.mkdir()
+    _save(output / "protocol.json", {
+        "command": [sys.executable, str(Path(__file__).resolve()), *sys.argv[1:]],
+        "historical_seeds": HISTORICAL_SEEDS, "derived_seeds": DERIVED_SEEDS,
+        "expected_case_count": 45, "expected_searches": 360,
+        "historical_input_policy": "35 original small_case(seed) configurations unchanged",
+        "derived_case_counts": {"stationary_first_kernel": 5, "synthetic_particle": 5},
+        "windows": "[0,T] and [1,T-1] with original endpoints and full fixed suffix",
+        "modes": MODES, "tolerance": ATOL, "search_limits": None,
+        "data_type": "synthetic_toy", "global_epsilon_certified": False,
+        "scope": "finite numerical optimality for each fixed-endpoint window only",
+        "source_sha256": {str(path.relative_to(ROOT)): _sha(path) for path in (
+            Path(__file__).resolve(), ROOT / "scripts/stdc_validation_guards.py",
+            ROOT / "scripts/run_stdc_small_search.py", ROOT / "src/asar_repro/window_search.py",
+            ROOT / "src/asar_repro/window_bounds.py", ROOT / "src/asar_repro/objective.py",
+            ROOT / "src/asar_repro/motion.py",
+        )},
+    })
+    rows = []
+    completed_cases = []
+    current = None
+    started = perf_counter()
+    try:
+        with (output / "results.jsonl").open("w", encoding="utf-8", buffering=1) as stream:
+            for kind, seed, grid, cfg, derivation in cases():
+                label = f"{kind}_{seed}"
+                current = {"kind": kind, "seed": seed}
+                input_sha = freeze_case(inputs, label, grid, cfg)
+                path = reference_path(grid, cfg, seed)
+                initial = score_path(grid, path, **cfg)
+                windows = [(0, cfg["budget"])]
+                if cfg["budget"] >= 3:
+                    windows.append((1, cfg["budget"] - 1))
+                route_file = inputs / f"{label}_route.json"
+                _save(route_file, {"seed": seed, "kind": kind,
+                                   "reference_path": path, "windows": windows,
+                                   "derivation": derivation, "data_type": "synthetic_toy"})
+                route_sha = _sha(route_file)
+                for a, b in windows:
+                    current = {"kind": kind, "seed": seed, "window": [a, b]}
+                    _save(output / "last_checked.json", {"stage": "oracle_start", **current})
+                    oracle_started = perf_counter()
+                    oracle = independent_window_oracle(grid, cfg, path, a, b)
+                    oracle_wall = perf_counter() - oracle_started
+                    for mode in MODES:
+                        current = {"kind": kind, "seed": seed, "window": [a, b], "mode": mode}
+                        _save(output / "last_checked.json", {"stage": "search_start", **current})
+                        tic = perf_counter()
+                        result = solve_window(grid, **cfg, path=path, a=a, b=b, mode=mode)
+                        wall = perf_counter() - tic
+                        _require(result.path is not None, f"missing complete incumbent: {current}")
+                        candidate = tuple(result.path)
+                        # Full frozen replay independently validates all route edges and t=0.
+                        score = score_path(grid, candidate, **cfg)
+                        raw_result = asdict(result) if is_dataclass(result) else vars(result)
+                        checks = {
+                            "completed": result.status == "completed",
+                            "no_budget_stop_reason": result.stop_reason is None,
+                            "not_globally_certified": result.theory_certified is False,
+                            "full_absolute_horizon": len(candidate) == cfg["budget"] + 1,
+                            "fixed_prefix_preserved": candidate[:a + 1] == path[:a + 1],
+                            "fixed_endpoint_and_suffix_preserved": candidate[b:] == path[b:],
+                            "J_replay": abs(score.J - result.J) <= ATOL,
+                            "Pd_replay": abs(score.pd_final - result.Pd) <= ATOL,
+                            "optimal_window_J": abs(score.J - oracle["J"]) <= ATOL,
+                            "nonworsening_full_J": score.J <= initial.J + ATOL,
+                            "initial_no_detection": score.g[0] == 0 and abs(score.survival[0] - 1) <= ATOL,
+                            "mass_monotonic": float(np.max(np.diff(score.survival), initial=0)) <= ATOL,
+                        }
+                        row = {**current, "input_sha256": input_sha,
+                               "route_input_sha256": route_sha, "data_type": "synthetic_toy",
+                               "derivation": derivation, "reference_path": path,
+                               "initial_J": initial.J, "initial_Pd": initial.pd_final,
+                               "oracle": oracle, "oracle_wall_s": oracle_wall,
+                               "result": raw_result, "search_wall_s": wall,
+                               "replay_J": score.J, "replay_Pd": score.pd_final,
+                               "J_minus_oracle": score.J - oracle["J"],
+                               "J_replay_error": abs(score.J - result.J),
+                               "Pd_replay_error": abs(score.pd_final - result.Pd),
+                               "checks": checks, "status": "passed" if all(checks.values()) else "blocked"}
+                        _save(output / "last_checked.json", row)
+                        stream.write(json.dumps(_native(row), ensure_ascii=False, allow_nan=False) + "\n")
+                        _require(all(checks.values()), f"window search gate failed: {current}; {checks}")
+                        rows.append(row)
+                completed_cases.append(current["kind"] + "/" + str(seed))
+                if len(completed_cases) % 5 == 0:
+                    print(f"validated {len(completed_cases)}/45 window cases; searches={len(rows)}", flush=True)
+        _require(len(completed_cases) == 45 and len(rows) == 360, "incomplete window search audit")
+        aggregate = []
+        for kind in ("historical_dynamic_matrix", "derived_stationary_matrix", "derived_synthetic_particle"):
+            for mode in MODES:
+                group = [row for row in rows if row["kind"] == kind and row["mode"] == mode]
+                aggregate.append({
+                    "kind": kind, "mode": mode, "searches": len(group),
+                    "mean_search_wall_s": float(np.mean([row["search_wall_s"] for row in group])),
+                    "mean_expanded": float(np.mean([row["result"]["expanded"] for row in group])),
+                    "max_absolute_J_minus_oracle": max(abs(row["J_minus_oracle"]) for row in group),
+                    "max_J_replay_error": max(row["J_replay_error"] for row in group),
+                    "max_Pd_replay_error": max(row["Pd_replay_error"] for row in group),
+                })
+        summary = {
+            "status": "passed", "cases": len(completed_cases), "searches": len(rows),
+            "case_counts": {"historical_dynamic_matrix": 35, "derived_stationary_matrix": 5,
+                            "derived_synthetic_particle": 5},
+            "historical_seeds": HISTORICAL_SEEDS, "derived_seeds": DERIVED_SEEDS,
+            "tolerance": ATOL, "data_type": "synthetic_toy",
+            "global_epsilon_certified": False,
+            "scope": "all modes match an independently enumerated fixed-window optimum on these toys",
+            "independent_full_path_replays": len(rows), "aggregate": aggregate,
+            "total_wall_s": perf_counter() - started,
+            "max_absolute_J_minus_oracle": max(abs(row["J_minus_oracle"]) for row in rows),
+            "max_J_replay_error": max(row["J_replay_error"] for row in rows),
+            "max_Pd_replay_error": max(row["Pd_replay_error"] for row in rows),
+        }
+        _save(output / "summary.json", summary)
+        print(json.dumps({key: summary[key] for key in ("status", "cases", "searches",
+                                                       "max_absolute_J_minus_oracle")}, allow_nan=False), flush=True)
+    except Exception as exc:
+        _save(output / "summary.json", {
+            "status": "blocked", "completed_cases": completed_cases,
+            "completed_searches": len(rows), "current": current,
+            "error_type": type(exc).__name__, "error": str(exc),
+            "data_type": "synthetic_toy", "global_epsilon_certified": False,
+        })
+        (output / "failure_traceback.txt").write_text(traceback.format_exc(), encoding="utf-8")
+        print(f"blocked: {type(exc).__name__}: {exc}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
+        raise
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()

